# Code owners for kepr.
#
# Any PR touching these paths requires review from a listed owner before it
# can be merged (assuming branch protection is enabled with "require review
# from Code Owners"). This is the second half of the supply-chain defence:
# SHA-pinned actions close the external attack vector, CODEOWNERS + branch
# protection closes the internal one.
#
# Paths listed here are those that affect what ships in a signed release or
# how the daemon runs:
#   - .github/workflows/  — builds, signs, and publishes release artefacts
#   - Cargo.{toml,lock}   — direct and resolved dependency graph
#   - packaging/          — deb/rpm postinst, postrm, systemd wiring
#   - systemd/            — unit file, sandbox hardening
#   - install.sh          — install-time behaviour
#
# Note: review & merge still requires GitHub branch protection to be configured
# on `main` with:
#   - Require pull request reviews before merging
#   - Require review from Code Owners
#   - Require status checks to pass (CI, Security)
#   - Require signed commits (optional but recommended)

.github/workflows/  @justdoGIT
.github/CODEOWNERS  @justdoGIT
.github/dependabot.yml @justdoGIT
Cargo.toml          @justdoGIT
Cargo.lock          @justdoGIT
packaging/          @justdoGIT
systemd/            @justdoGIT
install.sh          @justdoGIT
